  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aZ4qgxGn5yHXXuqm-q1XvSjzV0mTBQH4BnmQGXlJins.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\nAn ideal gas undergoes a cyclic transformation starting from the point $A$ and coming back to the same point by tracing the path $\\mathrm{A} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{D} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{A}$ as shown in the three cases above.\n\nChoose the correct option regarding $\\Delta \\mathrm{U}$ :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "m5aGh",
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-I $)=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-II $)=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-III $)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cqgPS",
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-I $)\\gt\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-III $)\\gt\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-II $)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "roElj",
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-III $)\\gt\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-II $)\\gt\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-I $)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "q0EQu",
      "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-I $)\\gt\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-II $)\\gt\\Delta \\mathrm{U}($ Case-III $)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As internal energy ' $U$ ' is a state function, its cyclic integral must be zero in a cyclic process\n$\\therefore \\Delta U \\text { case }(I)=\\Delta U \\text { case }(\\text { II })=\\Delta U \\text { case }(\\text { III })$",
    "image": null
  },
